WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:10.190
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one glows amber beside a 3D slate-and-cyan torus ring where ordinary digital lock icons turn rose while one emerald pad lock stays sealed.

2
00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:17.812
<v Presenter>First, inside a mathematical time loop, almost every digital lock would break at once except a one-time secret pad.

3
00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:26.792
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two turns cyan as backward-pointing rose signal arrows vanish against a solid emerald causal barrier across the torus.

4
00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:35.170
<v Presenter>Second, in known physics, no quantum trick, analog circuit, or reported anomaly sends readable answers backward in time.

5
00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:44.186
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three locks in emerald beside a steep upfront-work curve and thirty-one glowing proof badges confirming zero time shortcuts.

6
00:00:44.526 --> 00:00:51.698
<v Presenter>Third, every fast lookup of a future answer is work paid upfront, which fresh random values defeat immediately.
